# Frontend conventions

## Routing

- File-based routes under `src/routes/` — do not hand-edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts`.
- Heavy pages (`catalog`, `team-management`, `certification-management`) use `lazyRouteComponent` with a **named export** on the page module. Keep those named exports; do not “clean” them as unused.
- Root shell / auth gate: `@src/routes/__root.tsx` + `@src/components/shell/`.

## Components

- Prefer existing components under `src/components/{admin,catalog,dashboard,pages,sections,shell}/`.
- Use Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes already present in the app (slate/blue shell patterns). Do not introduce a second design system.
- Client CSRF mutations: `fetchWithCsrf` from `@src/lib/csrf.ts`.
- Permissions: `@src/hooks/usePermissions.ts` and roles from `@src/lib/roles.ts`.

## Server boundary

- Never import `*.server.ts` modules into client components or route modules that ship to the browser.
- Logging on the client uses `@src/lib/logging.client-stub.ts` (Vite stubs server logging).

## Data fetching

- Prefer TanStack Query patterns already used in page components; hit `/api/*` routes rather than inventing parallel server-fn call sites unless the file already uses `createServerFn`.

## Styling

- Follow existing spacing/typography in shell and section components.
- Icons: `lucide-react` (already a dependency).
